(  1. ARITHMETIC PROGRESSION: NTH TERM) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(  1. FORMULA: a_n = a_1 + \(n - 1\)d.) Tj
T*
(  2. CONCEPT: The nth value in a sequence where every step adds the same difference d.) Tj
T*
(  3. INTUITION: Starting at a_1, reaching the nth item requires n - 1 jumps, and each jump changes the) Tj
T*
(    value by d.) Tj
T*
(  4. DSA CONNECTION: Arrays, arithmetic sequences, missing numbers, binary search on positions,) Tj
T*
(    simulation compression.) Tj
T*
(  5. INTERVIEW PROBLEMS: Missing Number \(LC 268\), Arithmetic Slices \(LC 413\), Can Make Arithmetic) Tj
T*
(    Progression \(LC 1502\).) Tj
T*
(  6. PATTERN RECOGNITION: If values increase by a constant gap, or positions map linearly to values, use) Tj
T*
(    AP.) Tj
T*
(  7. VISUALIZATION: 2, 5, 8, 11 has a_1 = 2, d = 3; item 4 is 2 + 3*3 = 11.) Tj
T*
(  8. COMMON MISTAKES: Using nd instead of \(n - 1\)d; mixing 0-indexed and 1-indexed formulas.) Tj
T*
(  9. MEMORY TRICK: "First plus jumps"; there are one fewer jumps than items.) Tj
T*
(  10. IMPLEMENTATION IMPACT: Replaces iterative stepping over all positions with O\(1\) direct) Tj
T*
(    computation.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(  2. ARITHMETIC PROGRESSION: SUM) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(  1. FORMULA: S_n = n\(a_1 + a_n\) / 2 = n\(2a_1 + \(n - 1\)d\) / 2.) Tj
T*
(  2. CONCEPT: The total of equally spaced numbers.) Tj
T*
(  3. INTUITION: Pair the first and last terms: each pair sums to a_1 + a_n, and there are n / 2 pairs.) Tj
T*
