(  6. PATTERN RECOGNITION: Read constraints before choosing approach.) Tj
T*
(  7. VISUALIZATION: n <= 20 may allow 2^n; n <= 10^5 usually needs O\(n log n\) or O\(n\).) Tj
T*
(  8. COMMON MISTAKES: Designing O\(n^2\) for n=10^5.) Tj
T*
(  9. MEMORY TRICK: "Constraints whisper the algorithm.") Tj
T*
(  10. IMPLEMENTATION IMPACT: Prevents overengineering small constraints and under-optimizing large ones.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(  121. HASH TABLE EXPECTED COMPLEXITY) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(  1. FORMULA: Expected O\(1\) insert/find/delete under good hashing and bounded load factor; worst-case) Tj
T*
(    O\(n\).) Tj
T*
(  2. CONCEPT: Hashing spreads keys into buckets.) Tj
T*
(  3. INTUITION: With uniform distribution, each bucket has constant expected length.) Tj
T*
(  4. DSA CONNECTION: HashMap, HashSet, frequency counting, prefix maps.) Tj
T*
(  5. INTERVIEW PROBLEMS: Two Sum \(LC 1\), Longest Consecutive Sequence \(LC 128\), Subarray Sum Equals K) Tj
T*
(    \(LC 560\).) Tj
T*
(  6. PATTERN RECOGNITION: Need fast membership, frequency, or first-seen lookup.) Tj
T*
(  7. VISUALIZATION: Keys are balls thrown into many buckets; low load means few collisions.) Tj
T*
(  8. COMMON MISTAKES: Ignoring worst-case collision attacks in system-level settings; mutating keys) Tj
T*
(    after insertion.) Tj
T*
(  9. MEMORY TRICK: "HashMap trades order for average O\(1\).") Tj
T*
(  10. IMPLEMENTATION IMPACT: Replaces nested searches with single-pass lookup patterns.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(  122. NUMERIC OVERFLOW BOUNDS) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(  1. FORMULA: 32-bit signed int max 2^31 - 1; 64-bit signed long max 2^63 - 1.) Tj
T*
(  2. CONCEPT: Fixed-width integers wrap or overflow beyond their range.) Tj
T*
(  3. INTUITION: Bits store finite states; arithmetic can exceed representable values.) Tj
T*
(  4. DSA CONNECTION: Binary search midpoints, products, sums, modular arithmetic.) Tj
T*
(  5. INTERVIEW PROBLEMS: Reverse Integer \(LC 7\), Pow\(x,n\) \(LC 50\), mySqrt \(LC 69\).) Tj
T*
(  6. PATTERN RECOGNITION: Multiplication of values up to 10^9, summing many ints, midpoint calculation.) Tj
T*
(  7. VISUALIZATION: mid = \(lo + hi\) / 2 can overflow; lo + \(hi - lo\)/2 is safe.) Tj
T*
(  8. COMMON MISTAKES: Casting after multiplication; cast before: \(long\)a * b.) Tj
T*
(  9. MEMORY TRICK: "Widen before multiply.") Tj
T*
(  10. IMPLEMENTATION IMPACT: Prevents silent wrong answers in otherwise correct algorithms.) Tj
